  "notes": "Godan verb ({五段|ごだん}). {薄|うす}まる → {薄|うす}まらない → {薄|うす}まって → {薄|うす}まった\n\nUSAGE:\nThe intransitive counterpart of {薄|うす}める (to dilute, to weaken). {薄|うす}まる describes the change happening on its own, while {薄|うす}める implies someone deliberately diluting something. Can be used for physical properties (flavor, color, concentration) and abstract qualities (memories, impressions, suspicion).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {味|あじ}が{薄|うす}まる: flavor becomes diluted\n- {記憶|きおく}が{薄|うす}まる: memories fade\n- {色|いろ}が{薄|うす}まる: color fades\n- {印象|いんしょう}が{薄|うす}まる: impression weakens",
